"site-links theming" is a notebook page
	<header level="1">
		Site links
		<header>Site links are the page shown's own links, for an app menu's end:  the real page it stands for (its `live` link, Fomantic UI's original for Spell UI's pages), and a way to report a problem with it.</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Set a public `--ui-*` token on the element, any ancestor or `:root`; it inherits into the shadow
			root. Edit a value below to try it.
		</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-site-links" playground>
				<ui-site-links current="#api" report="https://github.com/spell-app/spell-ui/issues/new?title={title}" pages="\[{ \"title\": \"Button\", \"href\": \"#usage\", \"live\": \"https://fomantic-ui.com/elements/button.html\", \"pages\": \[{ \"title\": \"API\", \"href\": \"#api\" }] }]"></>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			The theme menu above picks the theme for every page of the site:  Spell, Glass, Fruity or Merlot,
			each restyling this component through its tokens.
		</>
	</>
